Coverity: Make sure we never leak memory in default_hostname

Resolves:
	https://github.com/jhrozek/pam_hbac/issues/51
In particular:
	CID #82323

Coverity was complaining:
 89
   4. noescape: Resource hostname is not freed or pointed-to in gethostname.
 90    ret = gethostname(hostname, HOST_NAME_MAX);
   5. Condition ret == -1, taking true branch
 91    if (ret == -1) {
 92        ret = errno;
   6. Jumping to label done
 93        goto done;
 94    }
 95
 96    /* Make sure that returned string is terminated. */
 97    hostname[HOST_NAME_MAX-1] = '\0';
 98
 99    *_hostname = hostname;
100    ret = 0;
101
102done:
   7. Condition ret != 0, taking false branch
103    if (ret != 0) {
104        free(hostname);
105    }
   CID 82323 (#1 of 1): Resource leak (RESOURCE_LEAK)8. leaked_storage: Variable hostname going out of scope leaks the storage it points to.
106    return ret;
107}

As far as I can see this can happen only if gethostname() fails, but doesn't
set errno. To be on the safe side and have no Coverity warnings, add additional
defensive branch.
